# checks that our envelope structure is sensible when group syntax and
# domainless addresses are used. RFC 3501 defines that such that it
# isn't really, really, really possible. but. well.
depends empty-inbox
send 6
a append INBOX () {108+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@oryx.com>
To: stuff:;, nonsense
Date: Thu, 13 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

asdf
receive 4
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
a OK [APPENDUID 1 1] done
send 1
b fetch 1 envelope
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (ENVELOPE ("Thu, 13 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200" NIL (("Arnt Gulbrandsen" NIL "arnt" "oryx.com")) NIL NIL ((NIL NIL "stuff" NIL)(NIL NIL NIL NIL)(NIL NIL "nonsense" " ")) NIL NIL NIL NIL))
b OK done
end
